{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/984553-homebrew-revised-nimbus-tilt-rule","id":984553,"title":"[Homebrew] Revised Nimbus Tilt Rule","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-09T12:41:35-07:00","id":984553,"title":"[Homebrew] Revised Nimbus Tilt Rule","content":"Okay, so one of the additions 2e made, that I was quite pleased by in theory, was the Nimbus Tilt. I really dug the idea of a mage's personal magical signature having a real, tangible effect beyond pure flavour, that the mage could have a custom-built power emanating from their own identity and Gnosis. However, it's been incredibly clunky to implement the rules as written in my game, notably in cases where you have multiple mages co-ordinating in a fight. Nimbus Tilt quickly fell into the &quot;way too complicated to consistently maintain given benefits&quot; category of mechanics, even looking at the alternative voluntary flaring version of the thing for a turn. I'm sorry, but trying to maths out Potency of spells vs everyone's Resolves and record what Reach was used when so you know when a Tilt ends, <i>times</i> the number of mages there over the course of a fight, <i>and</i> asking whose willing to accept what and when, and dice rolling all the while... It gets complicated. <br /> <br /> This has saddened me. So I've made a revision I intend to try in my game from now in. It works like this: Nimbus flares as normal when you cast a spell, resist a supernatural effect, or voluntarily with a point of Mana. However, the <i>Tilt </i>of your Nimbus only comes into play when you spend a point of Mana and apply it to yourself or another individual in sensory range, one point of Mana per target. If your target is unwilling, roll Gnosis, try to beat or equal their Resolve. The Tilt lasts for your Gnosis in turns, and it's a reflexive action to apply. Two competing Tilts provoke Clash of Wills with highest Arcanum (or Resolve) + Gnosis. Applying a Nimbus Tilt is visible to Sleepers. <br /> <br /> This makes the Nimbus less of a chaotic representation of your magic, admittedly, but instead it makes it a <i>tool. </i>If you, with all your supernatural power decide, by gum, I want to be really good at this Skill or Attribute that's at the core of my persona, or knock aside certain Skills or Attributes in others that I loathe, then you can infuse your Gnosis with the power of the Supernal and stack the odds in your favour. But you also have to <i>choose </i>when you're invoking it, and it's pricey to do to several people and maintain. This makes it more tactical, IMHO, and hopefully will ensure it comes up in my game more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T11:04:15-07:00","id":984953,"title":"","content":"I can see the potential complications you've mentioned. I may have to use this for my next game. *yoink*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}